The source of deliver.c from cyrus-imap 2.1.18 includes this in option handling:
    case 'e':
        /* duplicate delivery. ignore */
        break;

The problem is that you don't switch to opened window, and webdriver searches for elements in the old page instead of the newly opened one.
Solution: 
String winHandleBefore = driver.getWindowHandle();
        for(String winHandle : driver.getWindowHandles()){
            driver.switchTo().window(winHandle);
        }

This java method's part switches to the newest window. Also consider maximizing it, because sometimes tests masses up in not maximized windows.
Another point: waiting. Try to read here about different types of wait. Good luck.

